{
  "schemaVersion": "2",
  "name": "Lab browser API: the person's ways out of a page state, Try again and Reload, Go back, and the page's own dialog answered Leave or Stay, each signed and only on a tab the signing device holds",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "description": "LAB-BROWSERAPI-8, board 10 (src/lab/browserapi.rs, Route::Reload, Route::Back, Route::Dialog and way_out; browser.rs's person_page): the agent's navigate to a site that refuses fails and the tab is failed. `POST …/reload` unsigned is refused (unsigned), with the job's token too (the agents' tools never get these routes); signed by a device on a tab nobody holds it is refused (not_held); once the device takes, another device is refused (not_holder); a reload while the site still refuses leaves the tab failed (browser); with the site fixed the same address loads and the tab is ready. Go back: the agent goes from the home page to the second, the device takes, `…/back` brings the home page back. The page's dialog: the agent clicks Leave, the page asks its confirm and the tab is in state dialog; the device takes, `…/dialog` {accept: false} is Stay (the page is still there, the dialog gone), with no dialog left a second answer is refused (no_dialog), and once the page asks again {accept: true} is Leave (the page goes home).",
  "trigger": {
    "manual": {}
  },
  "tags": [
    "lab"
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "id": "up",
      "use": "runtime.rust:lab.browserapi.up",
      "inputs": {
        "expect": {
          "paths": {
            "url": {
              "$contains": "http://127.0.0.1:"
            },
            "token": {
              "$type": "string"
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "d1",
      "use": "runtime.rust:lab.browserapi.device",
      "inputs": {
